        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: import zpool for writeconf_facet on ZFS",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: import zpool for writeconf_facet on ZFS\n\nwriteconf_facet stops the facet with -f, which exports the ZFS\npool unless KEEP_ZPOOL is set, then runs tunefs.lustre --writeconf\non a pool that is not imported. tunefs.lustre exits 19, and\nwriteconf_or_reformat falls back to \"tunefs.lustre failed,\nreformatting instead\", which costs a reformat and gen_config each\ntime.\n\nImport the pool before tunefs.lustre and, unless KEEP_ZPOOL is\nset, export it afterwards, leaving it as stop() left it.\n\nconf-sanity on ZFS in a test VM, 257 tests, before and after:\n13 tests (21c 29 35a 46a 50c 50d 50f 50g 51 57a 57b 59 64) logged\nthe reformat fallback before and none do after. Their total run\ntime went from 900s to 607s (about 22s per fallback avoided). All\n257 tests have the same result before and after (tests 36, 117\nand 158 fail both ways).\n\nAt about 13 fallbacks per run and 2400 ZFS conf-sanity runs per\n30 days, the VM figure is about 195 hours saved per 30 days; CI\nreformats are slower than the VM's, so the CI saving is larger.\n\nFixes: 9b1526b9431e (\"LU-3264 tests: support failover testing with ZFS\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity fstype=zfs\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-sec fstype=zfs\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I3967a42f4bfbea067eed49a44ac2255a36ab7709\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70209\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Arshad Hussain <arshad.hussain@aeoncomputing.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
